  <static seed="222" source="Contrib/DMOI/2-Sequences/2_6-Chapter_Summary/2_6_10.pg">
    <statement><p>Consider the recurrence relation <m>a_n = -3a_{n-1} + 10a_{n-2}</m> with first two terms <m>a_0 = 3</m> and <m>a_1 = 6\text{.}</m>
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Write out the first 5 terms of the sequence defined by this recurrence relation.</p>
<p><m>a_2 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <m>a_3 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <m>a_4 =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, ...</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solve the recurrence relation. That is, find a closed formula for <m>a_n\text{.}</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><m>a_n =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>12</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>24</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>48</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\cdot 2^{n}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The sequence is <m>3, 6, {12}, {24}, {48}, \ldots</m>.  It has closed formula <m>a_n = {3\cdot 2^{n}}</m>, using the characteristic root technique.</p>
</solution>
